    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (11 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on owners, formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nThe app generates its response DTOs from the OpenAPI spec at build time and maps them from the JPA entity via MapStruct, so I made two coordinated changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema (the response type, not the `OwnerFields` input type). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `displayName` field that appears in `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `getDisplayName()` method returning `getLastName() + \", \" + getFirstName()`. MapStruct's `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` mapping picks this up automatically by name.\n\nThe new `Cp05Tests` acceptance test passes (a `John` / `<lastName>` owner reads back as `\"<lastName>, John\"`), and all 11 tests across the suite remain green.",
